# Testing Playground

Interactive TDD bench. Attach this notebook to the running app
(**Runtime settings → Attached node**, name `financial_tracking@web.local`,
cookie = `LIVEBOOK_COOKIE`), sketch assertions here against the real
modules, then graduate them into `test/` where they run sandboxed and
gate commits.

> **Warning — no sandbox here.** The attached node is the **dev**
> environment talking to the **dev database**. Anything you insert or
> delete is real. DB-touching experiments below run inside a transaction
> that is deliberately rolled back; keep that habit. If dev data gets
> messy: `docker compose exec web mix ecto.reset`.

## Setup

```elixir
alias FinancialTracking.Repo
alias FinancialTracking.Tracker
alias FinancialTracking.Tracker.{ExecutiveBudget, Office, Purchase}

# Start ExUnit inside the notebook. auto_run: false lets us call
# ExUnit.run/0 explicitly, as many times as we like.
ExUnit.start(auto_run: false)
```

## Write tests in cells

Define (or redefine — just re-run the cell) a test module, then execute it
with `ExUnit.run()` in the next cell. This is the whole loop: tweak,
re-run, repeat.

```elixir
defmodule PlaygroundTest do
  use ExUnit.Case, async: false

  test "office changeset requires a name" do
    changeset = Office.changeset(%Office{}, %{})
    refute changeset.valid?
    assert {"can't be blank", _} = changeset.errors[:name]
  end

  test "purchase amount casts from string" do
    changeset = Purchase.changeset(%Purchase{}, %{name: "Pens", amount: "9.99"})
    assert changeset.changes.amount == Decimal.new("9.99")
  end
end

ExUnit.run()
```

## Database experiments (rollback pattern)

Wrap anything that writes in a transaction and roll it back at the end —
you get real constraint behavior (unique names, foreign keys) with zero
residue in the dev database.

```elixir
Repo.transaction(fn ->
  {:ok, parent} = Tracker.create_office(%{name: "Playground-#{System.unique_integer()}"})

  {:ok, child} =
    Tracker.create_office(%{
      name: "Playground-child-#{System.unique_integer()}",
      parent_id: parent.id
    })

  result = Tracker.get_office_with_children(parent.id)

  # Nothing above survives this line.
  Repo.rollback({:experiment_done, result, child.id})
end)
```

## Graduating a test

When a cell-test earns its keep:

1. Copy the `test "..."` block into the matching file under
   `test/financial_tracking/`.
2. Swap manual inserts for `FinancialTracking.TrackerFixtures` helpers —
   the real suite runs in the SQL Sandbox, so no rollback gymnastics needed.
3. Confirm it passes for real: `docker compose run --rm test`.
